error[E0960]: `hop x y` is not a type: it applies a relation to arguments
  --> tests/neg/p9g_locale.hgn:33:28
   |
33 |   inside : {x y : city} -> hop x y -> path x y -> Type. (*~ E0960 *)
   |                            ^^^^^^^ an applied relation
   |
   = note: as a meta type, an applied relation would be `⇑(r t̄)`, the lift of a fact type of an application, which no object term has: the fact type of a relation `r` is `r` alone
   = note: an applied relation is a proposition of the program that owns it: a relation of an instance, a module or a functor application `(f ā).r`, or one opened from an instance; a variable's relation is read by every program over it; a relation of the file, of a module body or of a functor's parameter is a proposition, written alone, in the declarations of that file or body
   = help: name the program with the turnstile: `P ⊢ hop x y`

